{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.6,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["U2", "J1", "R10"],
      "pins": ["U2.7", "J1.3"],
      "nets": ["NRST", "RESET"],
      "obs": "On the root sheet the MCU reset pin U2.7 is attached to a global label \"NRST\" (with R10 10 kΩ pulling it to VCC), while the Tag‑Connect header pin J1.3 is attached to a *different* global label \"RESET\". There is no wire or shared label joining them, so the programmer's reset pin sits on its own isolated net.",
      "exp": "The specification states the MCU reset net is shared with the header: \"R10 (10 kΩ) ties NRST to VCC ... NRST is also wired to J1 pin 3 (~{RESET})\". Both pins must carry the same net name so the SWD programmer can assert hardware reset.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Root sheet (PCB.kicad_sch): red global label \"NRST\" at U2 pin 7; red global label \"RESET\" at J1 pin 3 – no connecting wire between them"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Reset line: R10 (10 kΩ) ties NRST to VCC, holding the MCU's NRST pin high at idle; NRST is also wired to J1 pin 3 (~{RESET}) so the Tag-Connect programmer can pull it low."}
      ],
      "impact": "The Tag‑Connect SWD/JTAG probe cannot drive the board's hardware reset line; the MCU is held in reset only by R10 and cannot be reset by the programmer, breaking reliable programming/debugging of the board.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    },
    {
      "category": "missing_component",
      "components": ["R5", "U4", "C19"],
      "pins": ["U4.26"],
      "nets": ["U4.26", "GND"],
      "obs": "The display sheet shows no 390 kΩ resistor on the SSD1306 IREF pin; instead an extra 100 nF capacitor (C19) appears on the left‑hand bypass column that the specification's OLED network does not list, and the IREF bias resistor is absent.",
      "exp": "The specification's OLED bias network explicitly requires \"R5 (390 kΩ) — U4 IREF to GND\" to set the panel reference current.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "display.kicad_sch: left column capacitors C7 2.2u, C19 100n, C11 4.7u and flying caps C12/C13; no resistor labelled R5 / 390k anywhere on the sheet"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "R5 (390 kΩ) — U4 IREF to GND"}
      ],
      "impact": "With IREF left without its 390 kΩ bias resistor, the OLED's reference current is undefined, so the SSD1306 charge‑pump / panel drive current is wrong and the display may not light or may be overstressed.",
      "confidence": 0.45
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The build deviates from the reference in at least the reset path: the MCU's NRST net and the Tag‑Connect header's reset pin carry different global labels (\"NRST\" vs \"RESET\"), leaving the programmer's reset unconnected; the OLED IREF bias resistor R5 (390 kΩ) also appears to be missing. The remaining interfaces (I2C pull‑ups, BS0/BS1/BS2 strapping, TSC Rs/Cs, decoupling) match the specification."
}

